# Desperate Dinos (Ricochet Robots-style)

## Overview
Async multiplayer puzzle game. Each round shares one board layout; players solve independently within a time limit.

## Movement
- 16×16 grid, 4 colored dinos, walls, one goal cell per round.
- Tap a dino, then tap a cell in a cardinal direction; the dino slides until blocked.
- Each slide is one move.
- The dino matching the goal color must reach the goal to submit.

## Scoring
- Round winner: fewest moves; tie-break by fastest solve time (`time_spent_seconds`).
- Round winner earns +1 point on the game scoreboard.
- Forfeit/timeout counts as not winning the round.

## Rounds and timing
- Games have N rounds (`max_rounds`, typically 5–15).
- Creator sets **time per round in hours** (stored as seconds: hours × 3600; default 24h).
- Each player calls `start_player_round` when entering the round; clock starts per player.
- Round closes when all players submit or forfeit; results are then revealed to everyone.

## Privacy
- During an **active** round: opponents see only status (playing / finished / timed out), not move counts or times.
- After round `completed_at`: all players see full standings for that round.
- Cumulative game scores remain visible on the game details screen.

## Notifications
- Invited to a game
- Another player finished the current round (no move count in message)
- Round results ready for all players
- Game over
